WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
One course bans AI. Another requires it. A third allows it for some tasks. So what is the rule?

2
00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:15.942
The rule is the policy of the course you are in. Find it in the syllabus or the assignment, and ask your instructor if it is unclear.

3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.800
When AI is allowed, disclose it. Just saying I used AI tells your instructor almost nothing.

4
00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:28.817
A good disclosure says three things: what tool, for what, and what you did with the output.

5
00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:33.392
Keep a record of your key prompts, and of what you kept or changed.

6
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:41.642
Detectors make mistakes. If your work is questioned, your drafts and your record are the best evidence of your own process.

7
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.700
Pen out. Integrity has two parts.

8
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.700
A good disclosure has three parts.

9
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.650
And your record is your evidence.
